// Saturn V (1969).
// S-IC, S-II and S-IVB, then the lunar module, service module and command module. The lunar
// module rides as a payload stage below the CSM (the game can't turn the CSM around to dock
// with it).
// Built by hand from the generator's output. The S-IVB carries four APS thrusters for attitude
// control between its burns. The S-II lights from four solid ullage motors
// in the S-IC/S-II interstage and the S-IVB from two on its aft skirt, as the real ones did;
// a stage cannot start its J-2s without settled propellant (the S-IVB, with its two starts,
// settles for the second one with the service module's RCS, which carries the real CSM's
// 550 kg).
